# Python / Ruff

Follow `.ruff.toml`. Do not weaken rules ad hoc (no `# noqa` unless justified).

## Must

- Put `from __future__ import annotations` at the top of every module (isort `required-imports`).
- Use Ruff for lint + format (`line-length = 90`, target `py311`).
- FastAPI uploads/deps: `Annotated[UploadFile, File()]` / `Annotated[..., Depends(...)]` — avoid `= File(...)` defaults (B008).
- Leave line length to the formatter; do not fight E501 (ignored).

## Avoid

- Extra docstrings/comments that restate the code.
- Editing under `notebooks/` or `data/` (excluded from Ruff).
- Duplicating Ruff settings in `pyproject.toml` — config lives in `.ruff.toml` only.

## Hooks

Pre-commit runs `ruff` (`--fix`) then `ruff-format` (see `.pre-commit-config.yaml`).

```bash
uv run ruff check --fix .
uv run ruff format .
```
